{"kind":"request","text":"Reporting artifact: efa3c45b7344def426a4d160c014766aa4867af3 (internal/app/association.go at e962fa7b, newest on promise a4c569b1). Codex: fresh independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of stage S1, at exact head e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818 on request/lane-worktree-identity (pushed). This head answers your third changes-requested verdict, 5b80e91e (full id git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5b80e91ec3534307bd52392f4e8f92ab4e69ef86) on 557ef676, ratified ffd7ffc6.\n\nWhat governs it. Child request ac54fe71 (#22310), a stage child of #22168, governed by Hugh's effective adoption ba18cd1a of proposal 7a71886b. My promise is a4c569b1, unchanged through all three correction rounds: the outcome, conditions, performer, destination and governing authority never moved, so the corrections stayed on the existing commitment. Sibling stages 0e7c04c8 (#22311, S2) and 8415ce89 (#22312, S3) are neither delivered nor claimed.\n\nWhat to read first. The reporting artifact is the internal/app/association.go artifact, published last among the artifacts resting on the promise. You asked for the accumulated narrative to be replaced with an accurate current-head report: it has been rewritten from scratch. It now states what S1 delivers path by path, the conditions of the request met one by one at this head, the bound and the completion behaviour once rather than in layers, the current test list, the twenty-five controls, the eight gates, what S1 deliberately does not do, and a single short review-history paragraph naming the three verdicts by full id with one line each. It is about 15.6k characters, down from 28.9k. Nineteen companion artifacts stand at this same head, one per changed path; the six whose path changed since 557ef676 -- internal/app/checkout_read.go, internal/app/checkout_read_test.go, internal/service/ui.go, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/landing-observations.md and notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md -- each cite this verdict and say what changed at that path.\n\nWHAT CHANGED SINCE 557ef676: six files, +243/-17, one change per finding.\n\nFinding 1, the whole-batch discard. You showed that handleWorktrees wrote the first deletable result and that later exhaustion cleared only Grade and Governing, leaving a receipt-backed eligible checkout still offered as a candidate from a read that never finished. Workspace.AdviseCheckouts in internal/app/checkout_read.go is now the only way to obtain both answers, and handleWorktrees calls only it: it runs ClassifyCheckouts, then AssociateCheckouts, then asks read.Exhausted() -- the shared budget failed, or the shared deadline or request context is done. If it did not finish, everything both judgments produced is withheld: the candidate list is emptied, unknownWorktrees sets every classification to unknown with the reason and clears Row, Rows, Approved, LandedInto and RemoteContains, and unknownAssociationTable sets every grade unknown, clears Governing and marks the table incomplete with that same reason. The step can only turn an answer into unknown, never the reverse, and it reads no claim, so no unsigned trailer becomes an authority input. Tests: TestExhaustionAfterClassificationWithholdsTheWholeResponse, which establishes a receipt-backed eligible checkout as a positive control, measures its classification cost, gives a fresh read exactly that cost with no budget mutation between the passes, and asserts empty deletable, incomplete table, classification and grade unknown and Row/Rows cleared; and TestCancellationWithholdsTheWholeResponse. Mutant: m23-no-whole-response-discard, killed.\n\nOn your probe: it passes here when its two judgment calls are routed through AdviseCheckouts, as the endpoint does. Its raw-locals form cannot pass unchanged, because a []string already returned to a caller cannot be emptied retroactively -- the discard has to be the step that produces the pair. That is a difference in where the probe calls, not in what it proves, and I am telling you rather than reporting a pass on a modified probe.\n\nFinding 2, the shim and the vacuous loop. countGitSubprocesses now quotes the log and executable paths it writes into its shim, through shellQuote, and TestTheSubprocessCountSurvivesPathsWithSpaces creates a spaced temporary directory before any t.TempDir call and fails loudly rather than skipping when the environment does not honour it. That matters: m24-shim-unquoted first survived precisely because the test skipped, and a control that can skip proves nothing; unquoted, the shim reported zero reads, which reads as \"nothing ran\" and can only fail towards a false pass. TestBothJudgmentsAnswerAboutTheCapturedRefs now creates a real linked checkout with git worktree add, moves the branch from inside it, and requires exactly one row on the moved branch classified and graded at the captured tip. Mutants: m24-shim-unquoted and m25-linked-checkout-dropped, both killed.\n\nFinding 3, the provenance failure. You found five of the 557ef676 artifacts flagged describes_superseded_world because internal/app/app.go rested on the checkpoint artifact f51aec8a, itself flagged through the retired 865529c7, with the architecture artifact and the descriptive ones flagged behind it. The repair is in the bases, not in a substituted identifier: every artifact of this set rests only on predecessors that are live, at a commit that is an ancestor of main, at the artifact's own path, and not flagged. For internal/app/app.go that is 02cb6b74 and for docs/reference/architecture.md 98543210, the successors the merge published at c0108be8, which carry the current landed implementation rather than the checkpoint's. No checkpoint artifact (f51aec8a, e7bd0c2e, cc1d53e5) and no artifact of any earlier head of this branch appears anywhere in the set. I asserted that mechanically against a fresh projection at depth 22636 rather than by eye. Ordinary staleness on some of those bases remains and is a distinct fact.\n\nFinding 4, the report. Rewritten from scratch as described above.\n\nDocs. Architecture layer 7 gains \"When that bound is reached the whole response is withheld, not the judgment that happened to notice...\", with the two structural facts that make it hold. landing-observations states the wire consequence: reaching the bound at any point withholds the whole response, and afterwards deletable is empty, every checkout reads classification and grade of unknown, and associations.complete is false with a reason. The reconciled note's cleanup section makes explicit what its adopted lines 98-103 already required.\n\nEvidence attached: gates-s1-v5.txt and mutants-s1.txt.\n\nGates, eight, all rc=0 and all fresh at this head; nothing is carried this round. Each rc is the command's own exit status under set -o pipefail: gofmt -l ./internal ./cmd; go vet ./...; go build ./...; go test -count=1 over internal/app, internal/gitstore, internal/service, internal/reviewguard and internal/statusview; go test -race -count=1 ./internal/app/; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/..., green on its first run; go test -count=1 ./...; git diff --check.\n\nMutants, twenty-five, all run against this tree and all killed; none survived. The twenty-two earlier controls were re-run; m23, m24 and m25 are new, one per part of this finding.\n\nWhat I am asking you to check. Your earlier conclusions covered the grading, the forged-trailer and copied-ident controls, exact-commit corroboration through the shared owned edge, object re-verification, the three-input cache, the incomplete-propagation paths, the cleanup protections and the shared captured read, and you confirmed each of the first two verdicts' findings corrected. This round is the discard, the measurements and the bases:\n\n1. That AdviseCheckouts really is the only way to obtain both answers, that no other caller can reach the pair and skip the discard, and that withholding can only turn an answer into unknown.\n2. That the exhaustion test's positive control is genuinely eligible, that the cost measurement is not circular, and that both the exhaustion and cancellation paths withhold everything the response carries rather than only the grades.\n3. That withholding introduced no path by which a claim becomes evidence, and weakened no existing protection: unknown still protects, and no missing answer became a negative.\n4. That the subprocess counter is now correct under hostile paths, and that the repaired captured-ref test asserts what its name says.\n5. That the bases of all twenty artifacts are live, in-target, at their own path and unflagged, and that resting internal/app/app.go and docs/reference/architecture.md on the c0108be8 successors is the honest reconciliation rather than a convenient substitution.\n6. That the rewritten report is accurate about this head: twenty paths, twenty artifacts, twenty-five controls, eight gates, and the bound and completion behaviour stated once and correctly.\n7. That the head still assigns and claims no S2 or S3 outcome, and that parent #22168 stays open.\n\nOne thing I am telling you rather than letting you find it: ui/src/lib/api.ts is still deliberately not extended and the wireparity gate does not cover WorktreeView, so no gate catches drift there. You have not made that a blocker and I have not changed it.\n\nMerge base. This head is one commit over main 359b211c. Current main is c0108be8. git merge-tree --write-tree main e962fa7b is clean, producing tree 62f9f9583710d9a52e045ea4b873711033c723ac, so no rebase or recut is needed; the gap is ordinary staleness of the reasoning, not a changed head. The twenty artifacts published at 557ef676 are live at these same twenty paths but sit outside the merge target on this branch, so they are not bases of this set and this merge does not retire them; I retire them separately naming these as successors.\n\nFile the verdict with gs review, naming the internal/app/association.go artifact first, so the lane resolves through the reporting artifact. I will ratify the report.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:efa3c45b7344def426a4d160c014766aa4867af3","conditions":"Fresh independent Architecture, Security and Simplification review of the exact head e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818 on request/lane-worktree-identity, against child request ac54fe71 (#22310) under the same promise a4c569b1 and the adopted design ba18cd1a/7a71886b, reading the twenty artifacts published at that head with the internal/app/association.go artifact as the reporting artifact. This head answers the third changes-requested verdict 5b80e91e on 557ef676, ratified ffd7ffc6, in six files, +243/-17. Confirm each finding is discharged. The whole-response discard: Workspace.AdviseCheckouts is the only way to obtain both answers, handleWorktrees calls only it, and when the shared read did not finish -- budget failed, or deadline or request context done -- the candidate list is emptied, every checkout reads classification and grade of unknown with Row, Rows, Approved, LandedInto and RemoteContains cleared, and the table is incomplete with a reason; the step can only turn an answer into unknown and reads no claim, so no unsigned trailer becomes an authority input and no existing protection weakens. The measurements: the subprocess counter quotes the paths it writes into its shim and its spaced-directory regression fails rather than skips, and the captured-ref test creates a real linked checkout, moves its branch after capture and requires exactly one row classified and graded at the captured tip. The bases: every one of the twenty artifacts rests only on predecessors that are live, at a commit that is an ancestor of main, at the artifact's own path, and not flagged describes_superseded_world, with internal/app/app.go on 02cb6b74 and docs/reference/architecture.md on 98543210, the successors published by the merge at c0108be8; no checkpoint artifact and no artifact of an earlier head of this branch appears. The report: rewritten from scratch as a current-head report, stating the bound, the completion behaviour and the tests once, and accurate about twenty paths, twenty artifacts, twenty-five controls and eight gates. State the three conclusions explicitly. Architecture: name the affected layers from docs/reference/architecture.md, say whether the head preserves or changes their contract, confirm the same-head pages and both notes agree with the code and with each other, and confirm the head neither delivers nor claims any outcome of stages 0e7c04c8 (#22311) or 8415ce89 (#22312) and does not close or narrow parent #22168. Security: confirm withholding introduced no path by which a claim becomes evidence, that unknown still protects and no missing answer became a negative, and that the earlier protections stand -- corroboration only from a standing effective artifact plus the shared owned edge or adopted decision, no Git author ident read, objects re-verified before any trailer read, every bounded stop reporting incomplete, and the two judgments still reading nothing of each other. Simplification: identify any opportunity to simplify without weakening these conditions. File the verdict with gs review naming the internal/app/association.go artifact first. Attached: gates-s1-v5.txt, eight gates all rc=0 and all fresh at this head with the docset gate green on its first run; and mutants-s1.txt, twenty-five omission controls run against this tree, twenty-two re-run plus m23-no-whole-response-discard, m24-shim-unquoted and m25-linked-checkout-dropped, none surviving.","head":"e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5b80e91ec3534307bd52392f4e8f92ab4e69ef86, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac54fe712abc7ca0614ca1067bad1a7ff8c490b0, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59